  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 3.4.3, 'Hierarchical terminology content, from global reference standards to facility-level dictionaries, with top-down customisation and upward feedback', adapted from the OpenHIE National Health Data Dictionary (NHDD) framework (section 3.4.5). Titled 'NHDD Framework: Content Structure', it stacks five layers from top to bottom: Reference/Administrative Code Sets (for example SNOMED, ICD, HL7); Curated Concept Sources/Interface Terminologies (for example CIEL, IMO); Country-level Subsets/Customizations; Organization-level Dictionaries/Customizations; and Facility-level Dictionaries (for example formularies). A downward arrow on the left says that international standards are selected and customised for country use, then adapted further for local implementation. An upward arrow on the right reads 'Submissions / Feedback to Standards' and 'Responsive Local & National Governance'.",
